delf / unloadrt of a function while its thread is running.

The realtime thread walks its funct_list without the HAL mutex. Without
quiescence, hal_del_funct_from_thread() unlinks the entry (its links then
point to itself) and recycles it at once; a thread that is inside the
entry keeps calling it forever or follows a recycled link, and unloadrt
dlclose()s code the thread may still execute.

delftest.py holds the thread inside the function of delfvictim (input pin
hold) and runs delf, then unloadrt, from another process. Each must not
return while the thread is inside, must succeed after it is released, and
the thread must keep advancing threadbeat afterwards.
